// SOLO PIANO: every part of a written or imported piece on the piano (docs/design/music-page.md
// section 15a, rung 3a; the operator chose it first, 2026-11-20). The `piano` part plays the best
// installed piano recording (the core set's FreePats upright, CC0), the synthesised electric piano
// when none is installed.
//
// A full score becomes a PIANO REDUCTION (crate::style has the rules and why): every note folded into
// the piano's keys, a unison doubling struck once, at most ten keys down together (two hands) keeping
// the outer notes and every pitch class, and each chord voiced with its top note full, its bass a
// little under and its inner notes softer. A drum track is left out (a piano plays no drums), said in
// words on the piece's details.
Style(
    id: "solo_piano",
    words: "music.style.solo_piano",
    plain_words: "music.style.solo_piano_plain",
    level_db: 0.0,
    default: Some((instrument: "electric_piano", part: Some("piano"))),
    programs: [
        (from: 0, to: 127, voice: (instrument: "electric_piano", part: Some("piano"))),
    ],
    reduction: Some((max_notes: 10, low: "A0", high: "C8", together_ms: 30.0, top: 1.0, bottom: 0.9, inner: 0.75)),
)
